+## Fix round 2 — Reject the complete latest status family
+
+Scoped rereview found round 1 incomplete: the exclusion enumerated release/integration and still admitted milestone and custom statuses. [Gradle's primary metadata documentation](https://docs.gradle.org/current/userguide/component_metadata_rules.html) defines `latest.someStatus` selection, default integration/milestone/release statuses and custom status schemes. The source was read during this fix. Fix base: `fff70c0e14d50d68cdc77865cd8d123394a8d059`; verified 2026-10-06 around 06:16 UTC with the original environment and isolated test directories. This section supersedes round 1's completion assessment.
+
+The shared validator now rejects any `latest.` prefix case-insensitively, plus bare latest, without listing status names. The existing exact-version, prerelease and build-metadata acceptance behavior remains intact. Four added selector values (standard milestone in lower/uppercase and two arbitrary custom statuses with mixed casing) exercise artifact metadata and supplied constraints separately. All eight new cases failed before the validator change and passed afterward. Self-review checked that prefix rejection covers arbitrary status suffixes, while the version grammar and other contracts remain unchanged.
